# Dependencies — reinstall with `pnpm install` in firebase/ and firebase/functions/
node_modules/

# Live agent coordination board (see AGENTS.md). Describes in-flight work on one
# machine: it would conflict in every commit and means nothing in history. Both
# agents share the working directory, so the file on disk is already shared state.
.agent-status.md

# Secrets. The Firebase *web* config (apiKey, appId) in
# firebase/web/assets/firebaseWebConfig.js is deliberately NOT ignored — those
# ship in the browser bundle and are public by design; Firestore rules and API
# key referrer restrictions are what protect the project, not hiding them.
# These patterns are for real credentials, which must never be committed:
# Admin SDK service accounts grant full database access and bypass all rules.
.env
.env.*
*-adminsdk-*.json
*serviceAccount*.json
*service-account*.json
*.pem
*.p12

# Firebase CLI state
.firebase/
.firebaserc.local

# Logs (emulator, CLI debug output)
*.log

# Personal Claude Code settings — per-machine permission allowlist, and it
# records local absolute paths. Shared project config belongs in
# .claude/settings.json instead, which is committed.
# Trailing glob is load-bearing: writes land as settings.local.json.tmp.<pid>.<hash>
# first, and a bare filename pattern lets those temp files through.
.claude/settings.local.json*

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
